- # `↯/s.100.4` — `EmailAddress.Error`
+ # `↯/s.100.4` — `EmailAddress.Error`

- Raised when a value cannot be parsed as a valid email address.
+ Se lanza cuando un valor no se puede analizar como una dirección de correo electrónico válida.

- ## Cause
+ ## Causa

- Urticose validates email addresses against the syntax rules in
- RFC 5321 / 5322 (with practical relaxations). The message is `the
+ Urticose valida las direcciones de correo electrónico según las reglas de sintaxis de
+ RFC 5321 / 5322 (con relajaciones prácticas). El mensaje es `the

- email address is not valid because $reason`.
+ email address is not valid because $reason`.

- ## Variants
+ ## Variantes

- ```tabular
+ ```tabular

- column  Code
- column  Reason
- column  Meaning
- column  Message
- column  Resolution
- row  `↯/s.100.4.1`  `Empty`  The value is empty.  `[↯/s.100.4.1] the email address is not valid because it is empty`  Provide a non-empty address.
- row  `↯/s.100.4.2`  `InvalidDomain`  The domain part is neither a valid hostname nor a valid IP literal.  `[↯/s.100.4.2] the email address is not valid because the domain is not a valid hostname: the character _ is not allowed in a hostname`  Correct the domain syntax; consult the inner `HostnameError`/`IpAddress.Error` variant for specifics.
- row  `↯/s.100.4.3`  `LongLocalPart`  The local part exceeds 64 characters.  `[↯/s.100.4.3] the email address is not valid because the local part is more than 64 characters long`  Shorten the local part to at most 64 characters.
- row  `↯/s.100.4.4`  `TerminalPeriod`  The local part ends in a period.  `[↯/s.100.4.4] the email address is not valid because the local part ends in a period, which is not allowed`  Remove the trailing period.
- row  `↯/s.100.4.5`  `SuccessivePeriods`  The local part contains two adjacent periods.  `[↯/s.100.4.5] the email address is not valid because the local part contains two adjacent periods`  Remove one of the periods, or quote the local part if successive periods are required.
- row  `↯/s.100.4.6`  `InitialPeriod`  The local part starts with a period.  `[↯/s.100.4.6] the email address is not valid because the local part starts with a period, which is not allowed`  Remove the leading period.
- row  `↯/s.100.4.7`  `UnescapedQuote`  A double-quote in the local part was not escaped.  `[↯/s.100.4.7] the email address is not valid because the local part contains a quote character which is not escaped`  Either escape the quote with a backslash or use a properly quoted local part.
- row  `↯/s.100.4.8`  `UnclosedQuote`  The quoted local part has no closing quote.  `[↯/s.100.4.8] the email address is not valid because the quoted local part has no closing quote`  Add the missing `"`.
- row  `↯/s.100.4.9`  `MissingDomain`  The address has no domain part.  `[↯/s.100.4.9] the email address is not valid because the domain is missing`  Append `@` followed by the domain.
- row  `↯/s.100.4.10`  `MissingAtSymbol`  The address contains no `@`.  `[↯/s.100.4.10] the email address is not valid because the at-symbol is missing`  Insert `@` between the local part and the domain.
- row  `↯/s.100.4.11`  `UnclosedIpAddress`  The domain begins with `[` but does not end with `]`.  `[↯/s.100.4.11] the email address is not valid because the domain begins with [ but does not end with ]`  Close the IP-literal with `]`.
- row  `↯/s.100.4.12`  `InvalidChar`  The local part contains a character that is not allowed.  `[↯/s.100.4.12] the email address is not valid because the local part contains the character > which is not allowed`  Remove the offending character or quote the local part to permit it.
+ column  Código
+ column  Motivo
+ column  Significado
+ column  Mensaje
+ column  Solución
+ row  `↯/s.100.4.1`  `Empty`  El valor está vacío.  `[↯/s.100.4.1] the email address is not valid because it is empty`  Proporciona una dirección no vacía.
+ row  `↯/s.100.4.2`  `InvalidDomain`  La parte del dominio no es ni un nombre de host válido ni un literal IP válido.  `[↯/s.100.4.2] the email address is not valid because the domain is not a valid hostname: the character _ is not allowed in a hostname`  Corrige la sintaxis del dominio; consulta la variante interna de `HostnameError`/`IpAddress.Error` para los detalles.
+ row  `↯/s.100.4.3`  `LongLocalPart`  La parte local supera los 64 caracteres.  `[↯/s.100.4.3] the email address is not valid because the local part is more than 64 characters long`  Acorta la parte local a 64 caracteres como máximo.
+ row  `↯/s.100.4.4`  `TerminalPeriod`  La parte local termina en un punto.  `[↯/s.100.4.4] the email address is not valid because the local part ends in a period, which is not allowed`  Quita el punto final.
+ row  `↯/s.100.4.5`  `SuccessivePeriods`  La parte local contiene dos puntos adyacentes.  `[↯/s.100.4.5] the email address is not valid because the local part contains two adjacent periods`  Quita uno de los puntos, o pon la parte local entre comillas si se necesitan puntos seguidos.
+ row  `↯/s.100.4.6`  `InitialPeriod`  La parte local empieza por un punto.  `[↯/s.100.4.6] the email address is not valid because the local part starts with a period, which is not allowed`  Quita el punto inicial.
+ row  `↯/s.100.4.7`  `UnescapedQuote`  Unas comillas dobles en la parte local no estaban escapadas.  `[↯/s.100.4.7] the email address is not valid because the local part contains a quote character which is not escaped`  Escapa las comillas con una barra invertida o usa una parte local correctamente entrecomillada.
+ row  `↯/s.100.4.8`  `UnclosedQuote`  La parte local entrecomillada no tiene comillas de cierre.  `[↯/s.100.4.8] the email address is not valid because the quoted local part has no closing quote`  Añade el `"` que falta.
+ row  `↯/s.100.4.9`  `MissingDomain`  La dirección no tiene parte de dominio.  `[↯/s.100.4.9] the email address is not valid because the domain is missing`  Añade `@` seguido del dominio.
+ row  `↯/s.100.4.10`  `MissingAtSymbol`  La dirección no contiene ninguna `@`.  `[↯/s.100.4.10] the email address is not valid because the at-symbol is missing`  Inserta `@` entre la parte local y el dominio.
+ row  `↯/s.100.4.11`  `UnclosedIpAddress`  El dominio empieza por `[` pero no termina en `]`.  `[↯/s.100.4.11] the email address is not valid because the domain begins with [ but does not end with ]`  Cierra el literal IP con `]`.
+ row  `↯/s.100.4.12`  `InvalidChar`  La parte local contiene un carácter que no está permitido.  `[↯/s.100.4.12] the email address is not valid because the local part contains the character > which is not allowed`  Quita el carácter problemático o pon la parte local entre comillas para permitirlo.

